  "description": "The current team comprises John\u202fDoe (launchpad\u202fID *jdoe*, GitHub\u202fID *jdoeGH*) whose primary contact is john.doe@example.com and who is employed by Acme\u202fCorp until 2025\u2011Dec\u201131, as well as Alice\u202fSmith who can be reached at alice.smith@openstack.org. Our product roadmap includes two scheduled releases: version\u202fv1.0, slated to conclude on 2024\u2011Jul\u201115, and version\u202fv2.0, slated for 2025\u2011Jan\u201101.\n\nAcme\u202fCorp manages the domains *acme.com* and *acme.org*, while the OpenStack\u202fFoundation controls *openstack.org* and *lists.openstack.org* and is also known by the alias \u201cOSF\u201d. The Nova codebase is hosted at https://github.com/openstack/nova under the OpenStack organization, with the module name \u201cnova\u201d. For the v1.0 release the repository uses branch\u202fstable/2024.1, moving from tag\u202f17.0.0 to tag\u202f18.0.0, and it is also referenced by the alias \u201cnova\u2011api\u201d. Finally, our project taxonomy defines a \u201cLibrary\u201d type (ID\u202f*library*) covering the modules\u202fnova and\u202fneutron, and a \u201cService\u201d type (ID\u202f*service*), marked as a child type, covering the modules\u202fcinder and\u202fglance."
